@PushListener_HostAddress = http://localhost:8080

### Handshake — what a device sends on connect (options=all)
GET {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/iclock/cdata?SN=TEST0001&options=all&pushver=2.4.1

### Simulate a punch upload (ATTLOG) -- 1001 should match a real Employee.LegacyId in
### ScheduleAppDb if you want to see it actually land as a matchable punch; any numeric PIN
### will still be accepted and stored, it just won't match an employee in the app's reports.
POST {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/iclock/cdata?SN=TEST0001&table=ATTLOG
Content-Type: text/plain

1001	2026-07-08 08:01:15	0	1	0

### Re-send the same line -- should come back processed but the console log (and
### PunchRecordImportResult) should show it as a duplicate, not a second row.
POST {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/iclock/cdata?SN=TEST0001&table=ATTLOG
Content-Type: text/plain

1001	2026-07-08 08:01:15	0	1	0

### A PIN that isn't a plain integer -- should be skipped and counted, not stored as garbage.
POST {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/iclock/cdata?SN=TEST0001&table=ATTLOG
Content-Type: text/plain

VISITOR-42	2026-07-08 09:00:00	0	1	0

### Command poll — what a device sends periodically to check for queued commands.
### Replies OK if nothing's queued, or C:<id>:<text> if the admin API below queued
### something for this SN.
GET {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/iclock/getrequest?SN=TEST0001

### Heartbeat
GET {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/iclock/ping?SN=TEST0001

### --- Admin API (not part of the ADMS protocol -- for you/the Control Panel) ---

### Every device the listener has heard from
GET {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/admin/devices

### Browse stored punches -- sn/pin/startTime/endTime all optional
GET {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/admin/attendance?sn=TEST0001&take=100

### Same, filtered to one employee and a date range
GET {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/admin/attendance?pin=1001&startTime=2026-07-01 00:00:00&endTime=2026-07-31 23:59:59

### Queue a raw command -- picked up on TEST0001's next /iclock/getrequest poll
POST {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/admin/devices/TEST0001/command
Content-Type: text/plain

CHECK

### Ask a device to re-push its attendance history (everything, since no range given)
POST {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/admin/devices/TEST0001/resync-attendance

### The spec's other resync mechanism -- resets sync stamps to 0 and queues CHECK
POST {{PushListener_HostAddress}}/admin/devices/TEST0001/force-recheck

